#14000
The Great Tower of Xerxes - Level 1~
This area (14001-14084) is the first level of the Great Tower of Xerxes.

The connection points are as follows:

North of 14001 is to be connected to 14901 (the ancient road).
North of 14084 is to be connected to room 14101 (Level 2).

Because of the aura surrounding them, no mobiles on any level of the tower
may be summoned or portalled to, if you happen to be aware of any that can
be, please report it to me as a bug. With a few exceptions, most of the rooms
in the tower can be portalled to (but the mage will require a non-native as
a target). This is so there is a mechanism to get players into the tower
again if they die, with out having them skip any of the nasty parts I wen't
to so much trouble putting in :) 

This level of tower has a variety of aspects. Firstly, there is equipment
here for evil characters of moderate level(20th-30th). The equipment is of
decent quality, and thus the mobiles possessing it are'nt complete push overs.
Secoundly, there are quite a few smaller mobiles which should be useful for
xps(althou they will be over-loaded by groups). People coming here for xps
will need to be carefull to avoid the "equipment" mobiles, this will come
with a bit of experience of the area or a good sense of caution. Careless
(or perhaps malicous) players could unleash a demon of moderate power which
could wander this level. There is a guardian who will prevent people from
reaching the 2nd level unless they are good enough to survive there.

This area was written by Vex.
~
140 72 0 0 0 0 255 0
S
#14001
Entrance to the Great Tower of Xerxes~
Passing through the brazen portal, you find your self standing in a large
entrance hall. The walls are of featureless stone, in fact perfectly smooth.
You marvel at the craftsmanship of the stone masons who must have built this
place, to your eye it looks like the whole tower is formed from a single
piece of flawless stone. The sudden chill you feel is not just from the
draught of cooler air drifting from inside, you feel like you are being 
watched, studied dispassionately by some powerfull being. You faintly hear
mocking ethereal laughter, filled with malice. Perhaps you should seek 
adventure else where...
~
