#14029
A Small Shrine~
The walls of this room are made of expertly painted panels, creating a mural
running right round the place. At the southern end of the room, you can see
a regal statue of what looks like a stately king. The sensation of being
watched you felt earlier returns strongly, you feel the presence is angry
at your disturbing this place. This quickly passes how ever, leaving you
slightly shaken. The only exit lies north, back to the Pilgrim's Chamber.
~
140 8 0 0 0 0 255 0
D0
To the north you see a large stone chamber.
~
~
0 0 14025
E
panels mural~
Looking closely at the paintings you see they tell a kind of story, which
looks like it begins to the left of the entrance. A primitive tribe is 
depicted kneeling before a radiant figure, almost to bright to see. Further
on, you see the tribes people have become farmers, and a small village can be
seen in the background. Next you see what looks like a young man on atop a
high mountain, kneeling before the radiant figure once more. You see the 
apparently peacefull farming folk led to war by this young man on other 
tribes. A city is shown being built, and beyond you see massive foundations
for some huge structure. The radiant figure appears again, you can see it 
more clearly as a smiling woman, skin of purest white and eyes like flashing
diamonds. Her hands rest on the head of the young man shown earlier, and his
body is surrounded by a glowing aura. Many panels follow, showing the man
as a King of a mighty nation. You witness wars, famine, and in the background
the building of a mighty tower. Through out what would appear to be centuries,
the King remains physically unchanged. Only his facial expressions are 
different. Before he looked kindly and benevolent. Later, he looks grim and
at times mournfull. Then comes a panel where the sky is black and lightning
is seen flashing in the sky. The King is shown standing on the steps of a
great domed temple surrounded by gardens and a great gathering of his people
stand before him, looking up in awe. The next panel shows the King laughing at
the sky, while before him a terrible change is overcoming the people. The 
women are all being changed into horrible beasts, while the men can be seen 
looking on in horror. The next panel depicts the radiant Goddess appearing 
from inside the domed temple behind the King, the Goddess glares at the King,
but he is just laughing while the beasts who where once women wreak havoc 
among the men who are fleeing in all directions. The next panel shows the 
Goddess fighting the King, a shaft of shining light in her hand. The King is 
laughing still, and a black mace is raised in his hand to strike. The next  
panel shows the King triumphant, the body of the Goddess lying at his feet, 
while a robed man in priestly robes looks on in disbelief and horror. Another
panel depicts the King smirking as the robed man is changed into a ghastly
creature, a great floating ball with many eyes, which retreats into the Domed
Temple. Near the end of the mural, a panel shows the King carrying the Goddess
into a Great Tower beyond the city, it's not clear if she is alive or dead. 
The last panel shows the King atop the tower, tears streaming down his face.
~
S
